From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 21:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 160/185] The pause corrupts sometimes, and sometimes is
 disqualifying

v24 read cleanly on the console. v28 -- the same driver bytes -- listed
21 garbage directory entries on the same console, and the headless runs
had already shown that face. A configuration that passes one run and
fails the next was never a high-water mark; it was a coin flip that
landed well once, and reverting it on the emulator's evidence was the
right instinct executed with the wrong justification.

Mechanism, best supported: the firmware's command queue is one slot at
$5AF2. CDBPAUSE drains through it over several exchanges; the next
visit's ROMREADN posts into the same slot, and whether it lands on a
completed pause or clobbers a draining one depends on timing nobody
controls. Clean and garbage, from the same bytes.

So the pause is out and the always-playing state is in -- light on,
data right every time, the configuration both worlds have never once
shown corrupt. The light returns behind a completion-verified pause,
alone in its own build, when the baseline is settled.
---
 bios/scdapi.h  |  2 +-
 bios/segacd2.S | 33 +++++++++++----------------------
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index 559db4b..2d11ee4 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  28
+#define SCD_VERSION  29
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
diff --git a/bios/segacd2.S b/bios/segacd2.S
index 348d450..66402d4 100644
--- a/bios/segacd2.S
+++ b/bios/segacd2.S
@@ -780,29 +780,18 @@ brd_fail_read:
         // interrupt frame thrown away. Either way a5 and the scratch
         // stack are the only things it may assume, which is why the
         // stack it has to go back to lives at 44(a5) and not in a6.
-        // v24's pause, restored on the console owner's evidence.
-        //
-        // v24 on hardware: D: opened in one shot, files read correctly,
-        // and the access light went out after reads -- their words,
-        // "probably the best state yet". v25 removed the pause because
-        // a HEADLESS gpgx run showed FAT corruption after it -- but
-        // gpgx does not model the drive's pause hover (its own sync
-        // and latency gaps are documented all over this port), and no
-        // corruption was ever seen on hardware with v24. Reverting a
-        // hardware-confirmed state on emulator-only evidence was the
-        // wrong call, made worse by two more stacked changes on top.
-        // The hardware is the ground truth; the emulator's pause
-        // artifact is noted and gets to be wrong.
+        // No pause, and this time the evidence is complete. The pause
+        // corrupts SOMETIMES: v24 on the console read cleanly, v28 --
+        // the same driver bytes -- listed 21 garbage directory entries,
+        // and the headless runs showed the same garbage face. A state
+        // that passes one run and fails the next is a dice roll, and
+        // the mechanism fits the single-slot command queue at $5AF2:
+        // ROMREADN posted while the pause is still draining through
+        // that same slot clobbers it. The access light staying on is
+        // the cost of data that is right every time; the light comes
+        // back only behind a pause whose completion is verified, as
+        // its own change, alone in its own build.
 brd_park:
-        move.w  #0x0084,d0              // CDBPAUSE
-        move.w  d0,50(a5)
-        jsr     0x5F22
-        move.l  _segacd_bios_frames,d2
-        addq.l  #6,d2                   // ~0.1 s of exchanges
-        move.l  #0x60000,d3             // ...bounded by spin regardless
-1:      subq.l  #1,d3
-        beq     brd_done
-        cmp.l   _segacd_bios_frames,d2
         bhi     1b
 brd_done:
         ori.w   #0x0700,sr              // shut the door before swapping back
